'''Doctor K.O.''' (ドクターK.O., ''Dokutā K.O.'', '''Doctor K.O.''') is a [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] variant of [[Kang Roo]] introduced in [[Candy Paradise]]. They were added in [[Version 13.4 Update|Version 13.4]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Doctor K.O.
|image = E 692.png
|first appearance = '''ZL:''' [[Yogurt Archipelago|Sub-chapter 12 - Yogurt Archipelago]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL:''' [[Obvious Cache|Sub-chapter 17 - Obvious Cache]]
|money drop = 650¢ - 2,567¢
}}

==Enemy==
Doctor K.O. is essentially just a Red/Sage [[Shadow Boxer K]] with a slightly higher money drop, only 3 knockbacks and higher stats suited for a [[Zero Legends]] enemy, although they aren't even that high for a trait with so many strong counters. The most unique thing about them is the debuff resistance granted by their Sage type, which makes [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]] crowd-controllers like [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Enchantress Cat]] and [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] much less effective against them.

At 100% strength magnification, Doctor K.O. has 380k HP, putting them just shy of an unbuffed [[Bore]]'s 400k, and 29,368 DPS, surpassing even a 300% [[Shadow Boxer K]]'s 28,108.

==Strategy==
Doctor K.O. may resist status effects, but any units that can outrange and deal solid damage to Red enemies ([[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] or [[Bath Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Luxury Bath Cat]], for example) can still keep this menace from being too bad with their meager 170 range. However, any tankers such as [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] will need to be at a high level to stall Doctor K.O.'s high DPS, especially with their resistance to Weaken. [[Rapper Cat]] with their resistance to [[Red]] and sage slayer can perfectly stall Doctor K.O.

